Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Tree-level graviton scattering in quadratic gravity with FeynArts\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"33a08bf5-6de0-47ed-9256-5348dfdb315d"],

Cell["Calculate the four-graviton tree of quadratic gravity with the diagrams and helicity conventions of example 04. Generate the three exchanges and the contact off shell, then impose massless kinematics during each FORM contraction to manage RAM. The final comparisons use the GR amplitudes of example 04 with the two internal mass parameters kept symbolic. Start in a fresh kernel.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23ac9814-e838-4d6d-8ae5-a73ffd8390ab"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Initialisation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"969bf553-0af3-4cf7-a469-c87bf47dedfa"],

Cell["\<\
Start in a fresh kernel and evaluate section 1 as a group, including the definitions in its collapsed subsection. Load FeynGrav with FeynCalc-patched FeynArts, then \
initialise QuadraticGravity as both the classes model and the generic model. \
The external T[1] legs represent massless gravitons. The internal tensor line \
also carries the massive spin-2 and scalar poles. In four dimensions their \
squared masses are M2\.b2 and M0\.b2. The curvature-squared terms enter both \
the cubic and quartic vertices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d51480d8-8169-4e52-a1f4-e96a93898401"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$LoadAddOns", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\"\<FeynArts\>\"", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qgModel", "=", "\"\<QuadraticGravity\>\""}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FeynArts`InitializeModel", "[", 
   RowBox[{"qgModel", ",", 
    RowBox[{"FeynArts`GenericModel", "\[Rule]", "qgModel"}]}], "]"}], 
  ";"}]}], "Code",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b5fa09c5-9dc4-4073-bb74-92956f3f9415"],

